@@ -2,18 +2,39 @@
 
 This is the source code of [Fizzy](https://fizzy.do/), the Kanban tracking tool for issues and ideas by [37signals](https://37signals.com).
 
+## Deploying the open-source edition
+
+Fizzy includes a Kamal configuration for a small, single-server installation. The
+server needs Linux, Docker, and a DNS record for the hostname you plan to use.
+The web process and background jobs run in one container; SQLite, Solid Queue,
+Solid Cache, and uploaded files are kept in the `fizzy_storage` Docker volume.
+Kamal Proxy obtains and renews the HTTPS certificate.
+
+1. Fork the repository and edit `.kamal/deploy.yml`: set `image`, the server
+   hostname, `proxy.host`, and the SMTP settings.
+2. Export the corresponding registry and application secrets (or put their
+   values in your password manager): `KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD`,
+   `RAILS_MASTER_KEY`, `SECRET_KEY_BASE`, `MAILER_SMTP_USERNAME`, and
+   `MAILER_SMTP_PASSWORD`. The checked-in `.kamal/secrets` file is a template
+   and contains references to those environment variables, not secret values.
+3. Point DNS at the server, ensure ports 80 and 443 are reachable, and run:
+
+   ```sh
+   bin/kamal setup
+   ```
+
+The persistent volume must not be removed when upgrading. Normal `kamal deploy`
+operations replace the container without removing it.
 
 ## Development
 
 You are welcome -- and encouraged -- to modify Fizzy to your liking.
 Please see our [Development guide](docs/development.md) for how to get Fizzy set up for local development.
 
